;; ====================================================================
;;  STOCK  -  what's on the shelves
;; ====================================================================
;;  Edit this file right on the GitHub website (pencil icon), then press
;;  "Commit changes". The site updates by itself in a couple of minutes.
;;
;;  Anything after a ; on a line is a note to us. The site ignores it.
;;
;;  ADD AN ITEM
;;    Copy a whole item, from its { down to its }, and paste it
;;    just above the last ] at the bottom. Then change the words.
;;
;;  EDIT AN ITEM
;;    Change the words inside the "quotes", or the number after :price.
;;
;;  MARK AN ITEM SOLD OUT
;;    Change   :in-stock true   to   :in-stock false
;;    It moves to the end of the shelf with a SOLD OUT stamp.
;;    To bring it back, change it to true again.
;;
;;  REMOVE AN ITEM
;;    Delete it from its { down to its }.
;;    (Or put a ; at the start of every line to hide it for now.)
;;
;;  WHAT EACH LINE MEANS
;;    :name         the item's name, in "quotes"
;;    :description  one or two short sentences, in "quotes"
;;    :price        whole dollars, no $ sign, no quotes: 300
;;                  or write :ask to show "Ask us"
;;    :category     :jerky  :apples  :wood  :candles  :handmade
;;                  (pickles and snacks go under :jerky)
;;    :maker        :buck  :hunter  or  :both
;;    :in-stock     true or false
;;    :tag          OPTIONAL little stamp in "quotes", like "Fresh batch"
;;    :image        OPTIONAL photo, like "images/jerky.webp"
;;                  Upload the photo to the images folder first.
;;    :icon         OPTIONAL drawing, like "honey-jar-dipper"
;;                  Pick a name from the ICONS list below. Copy it exactly,
;;                  with the quotes and without ".svg".
;;
;;  WHICH PICTURE DOES AN ITEM SHOW?
;;    1. its :image photo, if it has one
;;    2. otherwise its :icon drawing, if it has one
;;    3. otherwise the drawing for its :category
;;    So a photo always wins. Leave out both and you still get a nice drawing.
;;
;;  ICONS  (copy a name into  :icon "..."  )
;;    Jerky & Snacks:  beef-jerky  smoked-sausages  dill-pickles-jar
;;                     popcorn-bag  trail-mix-bag  pickled-eggs-jar
;;    Caramel Apples:  caramel-apple  candy-apple  nut-caramel-apple
;;                     bitten-apple
;;    Wood Working:    pine-tree-wood-sign  cutting-board  rocking-chair
;;                     birdhouse  wooden-spoon-and-spatula  wooden-bench
;;                     picture-frame  walking-stick
;;    Candles & Wax:   pine-tree-jar-candle  pillar-candle  taper-candles
;;                     wax-melts-tin  lantern
;;    Handmade Goods:  basket-plant  pine-wreath  soap-bar  knitted-scarf
;;                     honey-jar-dipper  wooden-toy-horse  patchwork-quilt
;;    A name that isn't on this list stops the build, and the message
;;    suggests the closest ones.
;;
;;  KEEP THESE EXACT: the colons (:), the quotes ("), the brackets.
;;  If something is off, the build stops and tells you which item and
;;  what's wrong. The live site stays as it was. See README.md.
;; ====================================================================

